  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Electric Boat obligated $8.6B in FY2026 to date. Award activity totaled 243 awards and the average award size was $35.2M. Obligations were down 60.0% year over year. Fiscal obligations across recent years show multiyear scale: FY21 was $8.7B, FY22 was $9.4B, FY23 was $10.8B, FY24 was $8.6B, and FY25 was $21.4B, with FY26 returning to $8.6B to date. Engineering Services accounted for the largest share of FY2026 to date obligations at $6.9B, followed by Ship Building and Repairing at $1.7B. Several manufacturing and R&D NAICS categories appear at much smaller levels, including Instruments and Related Products Manufacturing for Measuring, Displaying, and Controlling Industrial Process Variables at $2.4M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $1.6M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have Electric Boat obligations trended recently?",
        "body": "Electric Boat obligations peaked at $21.4B in FY25 and fell to $8.6B in FY26 to date. FY21 through FY24 obligations were $8.7B, $9.4B, $10.8B, and $8.6B respectively. The current-year obligations were down 60.0% year over year. The FY26 to date total of $8.6B matches the full FY24 obligation level."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are Electric Boat’s largest markets right now?",
        "body": "Engineering Services is the largest market at $6.9B in FY2026 to date. Ship Building and Repairing is the next largest market at $1.7B. Several manufacturing and R&D markets register much smaller obligations, including categories at $2.4M, $1.6M, and $1.5M. The remaining NAICS entries range from $1.1M down to $317K."
      }
    ]
  },
